<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sutlej River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sutlej</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sutlej River is a river of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>. It formed the boundary between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> and British territory. Accounts of the Sikh Empire note its importance in the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sutlej-river.jpg" alt="Sutlej River" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darshan Simha · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_view_of_Sutlej_river_Himachal_Pradesh_India_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
